From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-surya: add a measured
 OCV-capacity table

Without a table the fuel gauge interpolates linearly between
voltage-min-design and voltage-max-design. A Li-ion cell is nowhere near
linear, and the error is worst exactly where it hurts: with 3.68 V of
open-circuit voltage this cell had 8% of its charge left and the linear model
reported 28%. The phone duly ran until it died while still showing 5%.

    OCV      real     linear    error
    4359 mV  100.0%    95.9%    -4.1
    3999 mV   66.2%    59.9%    -6.3
    3846 mV   45.3%    44.6%    -0.7
    3755 mV   23.4%    35.5%   +12.1
    3678 mV    8.5%    27.8%   +19.3

The table is measured on the device: one full discharge from charge
termination to shutdown, 4.7 h, 566 samples 30 s apart with the CPU pegged,
pairing the IR-compensated open-circuit voltage against charge obtained by
integrating the reported current. 100% is charge termination at rest, 0% is
where the phone powered off (3.39 V).

The IR compensation matters here: sampling the terminal voltage under a 0.5 A
load and calling it OCV would have shifted every point by roughly 100 mV.

Limitations, since they bound how far this should be trusted: it is a single
discharge at about 0.2C, the cell warmed from 32 to 52 degC along the way, and
the cell is an aftermarket BN57 rather than the original. The table is
therefore declared at 25 degC without having been taken there.

Signed-off-by: Eduardo García-Mádico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
index f7a1b1a08..224bb74dd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
@@ -393,6 +393,26 @@ wcd9375_tx: codec@0,3 {
 
 &battery {
 	charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <5160000>;
+
+	/*
+	 * Measured on this device with a single full discharge (4.7 h, 566 samples
+	 * 30 s apart, CPU pegged), pairing the IR-compensated OCV against charge
+	 * obtained by integrating the reported current. Without it the gauge falls
+	 * back to interpolating linearly between voltage-min/max-design, which for
+	 * a Li-ion cell is wrong where it matters most: at 3.68 V this cell had 8%
+	 * left and the linear model claimed 28%.
+	 *
+	 * 100% is charge termination at rest; 0% is where the phone shut down.
+	 * Taken between 32 and 52 degC, so it is declared at neither end of that.
+	 */
+	ocv-capacity-celsius = <25>;
+	ocv-capacity-table-0 = <4359467 100>, <4297247 95>, <4245243 90>,
+			       <4190931 85>, <4137044 80>, <4085408 75>,
+			       <4035377 70>, <3986195 65>, <3939826 60>,
+			       <3900698 55>, <3870600 50>, <3844828 45>,
+			       <3821301 40>, <3801150 35>, <3780796 30>,
+			       <3762045 25>, <3739337 20>, <3714180 15>,
+			       <3687610 10>, <3644253 5>,  <3390789 0>;
 };
 
 &cci0_i2c0 {
